{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789661309,"nonce":"Cs5lzvCFnvjtnLKWhXHRs/UtCeY=","title":"Decision: modeling sprints / cycles / iterations","message":"Both Jira (sprints) and Linear (cycles) have time-boxed iterations that churn weekly, so they cannot be static schema values. Options: (a) a free `text`/`ref` field mapped 1:1 to the remote sprint name and treated as opaque; (b) an `iteration` entity type with dates, referenced by relation; (c) derive iterations from dates on issues. Roadmapping is quarter-scale and weekly sync is date-driven, so (a) may be enough for v1.","files":null}]}